Package: vennabers
Title: Venn-Abers Classification and Regression Calibration
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("René-M.", "Kruse", email = "rene.marcel.kruse@protonmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1655-9776"))
Description: Calibrates the predictions of classification and regression
    models with Venn-Abers predictors. A Venn-Abers predictor turns the
    score of any model into a pair of probabilities that contains a
    calibrated value when the observations are independent and identically
    distributed (Vovk and Petej, 2014, <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1211.0025>);
    Inductive and Cross Venn-Abers predictors make this practical for large
    data sets (Vovk, Petej and Fedorova, 2015,
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1511.00213>). The package serves analysts and
    researchers who need calibrated probabilities or prediction bounds for
    binary classification, multiclass classification by one-vs-one coupling
    (Manokhin, 2017, <https://proceedings.mlr.press/v60/manokhin17a.html>)
    or one-vs-rest, and regression (Petej and Vovk, 2026,
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2605.06646>). Predictions of an existing model can
    be calibrated directly, or optional 'tidymodels' workflows fit the
    model, create the calibration splits and tune the complete procedure.
    Diagnostics include the Brier score, log loss, plots of fitted
    calibration maps and reliability diagrams with the CORP (consistent,
    optimally binned, reproducible and pool-adjacent-violators based) method
    of Dimitriadis, Gneiting and Jordan (2021) <doi:10.1073/pnas.2016191118>.
    Core results are checked against the 'Python' package 'venn-abers'; the
    installed file PARITY.md separates numerical parity from R extensions
    and documented deviations.
